\title{Sets of characters are compared in one pass and can be read one stretch at a time}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-17}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1057}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The equality of two \code{\verb~|CharSet~}s reads both sets in step through the iterator of \code{\verb~|WavlMap~}; it is about three times faster for sets of 2,000 stretches. \code{\verb~|CharSet::iter~} is new and yields the stretches in order, one at a time. \code{\verb~|spans~} and the UTF-8 translation read the stretches the same way. See [the measurements](design-wavl-walker-regex).}

\p{In review as \pr{1057}.}
